  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The energy strategy shall be implemented accordance with the approved Energy and Sustainability Statement (V1) prepared by PES Ltd and dated 26 March 2026. Prior to first occupation of the dwelling,' 'as-built' Standard Assessment \rProcedure (SAP) outputs must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing to demonstrate that proposed dwelling has achieved the targeted reduction in carbon dioxide (CO2) emissions. All of the approved measures must thereafter be retained for as long as the development is in existence.  \r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Prior to first occupation of the dwelling, a completed Water Efficiency Calculator for New Dwellings must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing to show that internal potable water consumption will be limited to no more than 110 litres per person per day (l/p/d) based on the Government's national calculation method for the purposes of Part G of the Building Regulations.  \r\rReason: To comply with Policy 33 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Sound insulation should be provided to ensure that the noise level of 35 dBLAeq,16 hour in living rooms and bedrooms during the daytime (0700 to 2300 hours) and 30 dBLAeq,8 hour and 45 dBLAFmax during the night time (2300 to 0700\rhours) in bedrooms in accordance with BS8233:2014. Where these levels cannot be met with windows open appropriate acoustic ventilation should be provided so that the room can be sufficiently ventilated. The acoustic performance of any passive vent, variable speed mechanical air supply unit or whole house ventilation must be sufficient to ensure that the noise level standards given above are not compromised.\r\rReason: To safeguard the living conditions and residential amenity of future occupiers, to comply with Policies 9 and 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Prior to first occupation of the residential unit, the dedicated cycle storage facilities and refuse/recycling stores shown on the approved plans shall be fully installed and made available for use. They shall thereafter be permanently retained for their intended purposes.\r\rReason: To ensure adequate cycle parking and waste management infrastructure is provided, to comply with Policies 28, 36 and 37 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and Policies T5 and D6 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Statement form.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12."
  ],
